# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why eol=lf and not the git default: several test fixtures are C# raw string
# literals (`"""..."""`) whose content includes the source file's own line
# endings, and the tests then do `.Replace("...\n", "")` against them. Under a
# CRLF checkout (Windows `core.autocrlf=true`) those literals contain \r\n, the
# replace silently matches nothing, and the assertion fails - 7 tests in
# FrontmatterTests/VaultConfigTests broke exactly this way. The CLI itself
# normalizes \r\n on read everywhere, so LF working-tree files cost nothing and
# keep the suite green on every platform, including the win-x64 target we ship.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets that must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
